    {
      "type": "teach",
      "title": "Write the sound, not the rule",
      "body": "English writes one “-ed” for three different sounds. Shavian writes what you say: 𐑤𐑫𐑒𐑑 ends in a t, 𐑢𐑪𐑯𐑑𐑩𐑛 in 𐑩𐑛. Say the word, listen to the last sound, write that. The same goes for the plural — 𐑚𐑫𐑒𐑕 hisses, 𐑢𐑻𐑛𐑟 buzzes."
